{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your doctors here. You were admitted for nausea and vomiting, especially in the mornings. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been going on for a few days now. I wake up and just start vomiting, even if I haven’t eaten. It feels just like my past episodes with gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned before that you saw blood in your vomit. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, just a little, pink-tinged. I was worried it might be serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s called hematemesis, and it can happen from irritation in the esophagus. We’re keeping an eye on it. For now, you’re not able to keep anything down, so we’re giving you fluids through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m on NPO, right? When can I start drinking again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with small sips once the nausea settles. We’ve given you Zofran through the IV, which should help. We also did a chest X-ray and an abdominal X-ray earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what did they show?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — no pneumonia, no blockage in your bowels, and no free air, which means no perforation. Your labs are mostly stable too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why am I still vomiting? Is it my diabetes again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar was 161 when you came in — not in DKA. We’re continuing your Lantus and sliding scale insulin. But since you’ve had this before, we’re thinking it could be related to your esophagus or stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Reglan before for gastroparesis, but my GI doctor stopped it recently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. And actually, past studies haven’t confirmed gastroparesis. So we’re considering other causes. Because of the blood in your vomit, we’re concerned about a small tear or irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Could that be serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely a small Mallory-Weiss tear from vomiting. Your hemoglobin is stable, so no active bleeding. But to be sure, GI wants to do an EGD — that’s an upper endoscopy — tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "An EGD? I’ve had one before. Is it necessary?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because of the blood. It will let us see if there’s inflammation, ulcers, or varices — which are swollen veins in the esophagus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Varices? I don’t have liver disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "True, but sometimes they can occur for other reasons. We’ll take a look and maybe a biopsy if needed. You’ll be sedated, so it won’t be uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I agree. And what about my back pain? It’s been worse with all this vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know you’re on Tramadol at home. Since you can’t take pills right now, we’re giving Dilaudid through your IV, diluted and slowly infused. Once you can eat, we’ll switch back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And my anxiety — I’ve been really stressed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2125-04-15 19:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still getting your Zoloft daily, and you can take Ativan as needed. We’ve also had social work check in with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2125-04-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well overnight — no vomiting. We’re going to do your EGD in a couple of hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2125-04-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any updates on my blood pressure? It’s been high lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2125-04-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your BP has been elevated even after the vomiting stopped — around 130s/90s. We’re starting to think it’s not just from nausea. We may need to start a blood pressure med."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2125-04-16 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d rather not take another pill, but if I need to, okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from your EGD. It went well. They found mild varices in your esophagus and some patchy areas in the stomach, but no active bleeding or ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Varices? Does that mean I have liver problems?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. They’re mild, and we don’t know the cause yet. Since you don’t have liver disease, we’ll need to follow up outpatient to check why they’re there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the blood in my vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely from the varices or a small tear from vomiting. No active bleeding now. We’ve held your aspirin for now, just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take that for my heart. Should I be worried about stopping it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s precautionary. You’ll discuss restarting it with your primary doctor after your varices are evaluated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Can I start drinking now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2125-04-16 12:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with ice chips and clear liquids. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance your diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You kept down apple juice and broth last night — great job. We’re moving you to full liquids today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My nausea is much better. What about my insulin? I noticed my sugars were high yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on your Lantus at night and sliding scale. But we noticed you had some sweets brought in — juice, pudding. That can spike your sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess I got hungry. But I didn’t think it was a big deal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It adds up. We had a dietitian talk to you yesterday about balanced choices, especially with diabetes and kidney concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she was helpful. I’ll try to do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Also, we started you on Lisinopril yesterday for your blood pressure. We’ll keep you on it and monitor your potassium and kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll take that at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2125-04-17 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 10 mg daily. We’ll check your labs at your follow-up to make sure it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well — no nausea, no pain, and you’re tolerating full liquids. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do after I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to follow up with your primary doctor this week. They’ll check your blood work because of the new blood pressure medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the varices?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll need a GI follow-up to evaluate them further. And discuss with your doctor when it’s safe to restart aspirin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I can go back to my regular insulin and Tramadol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2125-04-18 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home meds except aspirin. Take Prilosec daily, Zofran as needed for nausea, and Ativan for anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look good, and you’ve had no issues overnight. We’re clearing you to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Just remember: call your doctor this week, get your labs done, and follow up with GI about the varices."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And if I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use your Zofran. If it doesn’t help or you see blood, come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my blood pressure — should I monitor it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you can, that would help your doctor. Otherwise, they’ll check it at your visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I have a monitor at home. I’ll start using it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and we’ll see you around only if you need us — but hopefully not!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2125-04-19 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2125-04-15 18:48:00",
    "admission_end": "2125-04-19 14:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of chronic nausea and vomiting was admitted for several days of early morning vomiting, including a small amount of blood. She was unable to tolerate oral intake initially and was managed with IV fluids and anti-nausea medications. Imaging showed no acute abnormalities. An EGD revealed mild esophageal varices and stable gastric findings, with no active bleeding. Her aspirin was held due to hematemesis, and she was started on Lisinopril for newly recognized hypertension. Her diet was advanced as nausea resolved, and she tolerated full liquids by discharge. She was discharged home with plans to follow up for variceal evaluation, lab monitoring on Lisinopril, and discussion about restarting aspirin.",
    "problems": [
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Gastroesophageal laceration-hemorrhage syndrome",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal varices without mention of bleeding",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Backache, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
